      "key":"family_premises_and_scope",
      "statement":"Instance premises are: workspace material exceeds one actor's competence/context/tools/access envelope; evaluations are declared questions about a governed outcome; multiple frames and actors may overlap; workspace/topology/capabilities change between activations; actors may read owners and copied/projected/compressed surfaces. These are work conditions, not commitments derived from finitude. P0's named actor-change premise permits a different next actor to reacquire declared sources, not private memory; its open-world premise says the world is open. Engagement law supplies no application profile, role mapping, product-owned frame-basis binding, domain product, runtime, workflow or assurance implementation. Specialisations retain their own owners and neither enter nor amend this member by proximity or matching names. Imported concepts retain owner and meaning through reference-only import, granting no semantic/evaluation/operation/decision authority; refinements name their owner and map to the core.",
