      "key":"acquisition_and_activation_boundary",
      "statement":"Acquire inputs by exact identity only from the exact selected basis. Absence from view gives neither permission to read elsewhere nor evidence of absence; candidate source, moving selector and another basis cannot substitute. A stale, missing or question-insufficient derived surface requires direct acquisition of deciding owner sections. Acquisition is read-only and grants no role, operation or decision; return a missing binding with its outcome before dependent action. Activation binds exact subject/basis and loads declared material relations/evidence, never an undifferentiated workspace dump. A reusable declaration proves no particular activation correct. If no available frame/actor pair can lawfully evaluate, return out_of_frame or the refusal whose cause holds without implied-context continuation. Configuration allocates frame selection to actor or assigning authority.",
