      "key":"core_claims",
      "statement":"The ten claims state: no finite actor is presumed to attend to the whole material workspace; a useful frame is finite and sufficient for its declared evaluation family; evaluation determines attention; human authority may declare practical sets from practice without mechanical unique partition; overlap/composition/refinement/restriction/translation/succession are permitted and hierarchy optional; joint frame use does not require composing internal coordinates; coverage is workspace/outcome/inventory/basis/time-relative; breadth/usefulness/actor/technology gives selection or result no semantic/operation/decision authority; unknown and out-of-frame results are reconfiguration pressure, neither failed evaluations nor acceptance; historical failures/resets/invisible violations are improvement evidence. These claims add no rules beyond their cited laws.",
